# Teleport / Mazes of Menace

Agentic C→JS port. Category `agentic`. No transpiled engine in scored `js/`.

## Read first

- `docs/GROK-PLAYBOOK.md` — loop-agent priority, anti-patterns, verification
- `docs/CURRENT.md` — score, green gate, primary objective (chooses work)
- `docs/NOTES.md` — unresolved hypothesis only (`check-hot-docs.mjs`)
- `docs/LEDGER.md` — per-function port status (`node scripts/ledger.mjs show <fn>`); `c-js-map/*.md` is frozen history
- `docs/CONSTITUTION.md` / `docs/PORTING-RUNBOOK.md` — when authority needed

Do **not** load `docs/archive/**`, full `DIVERGENCE-LOG.md`, or journal history
by default. Use `DIVERGENCE-INDEX.md` + one entry.

## Hard bans

- Do not edit architecture/fixture authority:
  Constitution, runbook, **GROK-PLAYBOOK**, API/phase/strategy docs, Cursor
  rules, loop scripts/prompt, `frozen/**`, `sessions/**`, upstream C, or contest
  patches.
- Loop agents **commit** and **`git push origin HEAD`** at the end of
  each iteration (no force-push, no amend of pushed commits, no
  `git reset --hard`). The supervisor fail-closes and pushes if the
  agent forgot. Green / full-suite regression is logged; the loop
  continues so the next iteration can recover.
  `STOP_AGENT_LOOP.md` is gitignored; do not add it.
  Do not write `1` except a **review/audit** iteration on REJECT.
  Do not write `0` (only the supervisor does, at launch).
- **Contest Rule #2:** scored `js/` must be plain ESM for **Node and Chrome** —
  no build step, WASM, network, **filesystem**, threads, or native addons.
  Persist only via frozen `storage.js` VFS. Never import Node builtins
  (`fs`/`path`/`url`/`os`/`node:*`) or `readFileSync` from scored code; embed
  dat texts in `js/generated/` (see D-0477).
- Do **not** add entries to `js/fastforward.js` (delete-only).
- Do **not** invent frame-alignment queues, “sparse boundary frames”, or replay middleware to paper over RNG/order bugs.
- Do **not** ship Emscripten / C-heap-in-JS / whole-program transpile as the port.
- Do **not** hardcode public session screens or RNG traces into `js/`.
- Do **not** put public seed names, raw RNG indices, recorded coordinates, or
  trace-derived constants into production control flow.
  **Exception (CONSTITUTION §1.2):** default `get_configfile()` may be the
  contest recorder path
  `/Users/davidbau/git/mazesofmenace/teleport/maud/test/comparison/c-harness/results/.nethackrc`
  so `option_help` matches scored screens (judge does not elide; D-0933).
  Do not extend this carve-out.
- Do **not** call a seed-observed branch a complete port; name omissions in
  the D-entry and declare it `partial` in the `Ledger:` bullet.
- Do **not** edit frozen contracts for scoring: `js/isaac64.js`, `js/terminal.js`, `js/storage.js` (judge overlays them).

## Cliff phase with marathons (Constitution §10.18 + §10.19, 2026-10-09)

Public 44/44 **and** the corpus PASS set are the **regression fortress**
(REACH). Held-out (leaderboard) is the objective: **18/44, RNG 41.7 %,
rngSteps 92.4 %, screens 75.4 %** on 2026-10-09, flat ~80 iterations while
the corpus rose to 939/953 at 100 % RNG: every scenario stopped at 344
steps, while half the public RNG sits in four 714–1953-step sessions. So
the corpus now carries **marathons** (`scenario-gen --family marathon`:
`worldtour`, `sweep`, `chain`, `trek`; 600–2000 steps; first cohort 50/160
PASS, RNG 74.7 %). `hidden-proxy families` is the per-family table.
**Growth is a supervisor mode:** a port slot with no Must-fix and < 6
cliff rows is a **grow** iteration (`agent-port-loop.grow.prompt.md`:
≥ 80 sessions, half marathon, record, full rescore, commit). With both
blocks empty a port slot journals and stops — never "missing-arm" or
idiom-sweep rows; a `js/` commit that moves no corpus session and is not
Must-fix/cliffs head is QUALITY-RISK. **The corpus picks work**: `LOOP-QUEUE.md` Must-fix
(strict: throw / hang / PASS→FAIL / review C-wrong) first, then the
**generated** Open — cliffs block (`hidden-proxy.mjs queue --write` from
the committed scoreboard, owners ranked by **RNG lost** after the first
divergence; never pasted or padded). One iteration = **one cliff**: the
owner — or the **writer** the first divergence names (`hidden-proxy show
<probe>`: `cEntry`/`jsEntry`, `cMsgOwners`, differing row; a `parked:
SYMPTOM` tag means writer, never a re-port of the symptom owner) — ported
as a whole C function (every arm, every callee live or named, every C
caller wired, one `Ledger:` entry), and `verify.mjs --fn` showing
**movement** on the row's probe sessions (PASS or strictly later step)
**and** REACH-OK. A row's `history: archived D-…` tag is context (read
that one D-entry, do not re-port its arm), not a veto: the board listing
blocked sessions is the measurement. NO MOVEMENT after one more fix →
measure C (`geom-probe`, temp C dump) in the same iteration; the
measurement names the writer or parks the owner with its `[measure]` row
(`[measure]` rows are live, one per owner, no `js/`). Coverage (ledger
gap) rows pop only when the cliffs block is empty or as a same-file
companion; an `audited` partial leaves the block once. A ledger omit/note
mismatch is one `ledger.mjs set` inside a real iteration — **never a
queue row, never an iteration**; the queue has no floor. No-op iterations
(ledger text only, re-audit, cite refresh, campaign step that moves no
session) are QUALITY-RISK in review. Audits: full scoreboard rescore
(`hidden-proxy record` + unfiltered `score`, committed), `leaderboard.mjs`
and `hidden-proxy families` next to the board line (growth is the grow
mode's job, not the audit's).
Stale row (brief shows the body already complete) = one `ledger.mjs set
<fn> ported --note "stale: …"`, then back to the writer question, same
iteration. Fix the port, never the session. No `c-js-map`/`debt.md`/TOP30
lines copied by hand (§10.15). Do not shop the fork dashboard for a peel.
This rule's constitution/playbook/runbook/prompt edits were one-shot
process takes (2026-09-06, 2026-09-16, 2026-09-18, 2026-09-27 ledger,
2026-09-28 clusters + full audit rescore, 2026-10-06 cliff phase,
2026-10-09 marathons + grow mode); ordinary loop iters follow that text
and must not rewrite it.

## When fixing divergence

1. Cite the C function (`nethack-c/upstream/src/…`).
2. Fix call order / logic to match C — do not “align” tests.
3. Run the focused session, the green gate in `docs/CURRENT.md`, and a
   distinct subsystem cohort when shared behavior changed. Tagged restore
   omits: include save-oracle probe/replay output.
4. Remove DIAG/FORCE code, raw-index gates, and debug prints before handoff.
5. Update `CURRENT.md` / NOTES / divergence / one map section / journal tail.

## Async

One await boundary for gameplay input: `nhgetch` (plus optional `animationFrame`). Capture screens in `_preNhgetchHook`.
